.TH YUME-GUI 1 "2026-08-23" "YUME 0.3.0-dev1" "YUME Manual"
.SH NAME
yume-gui \- desktop UI for the YUME post-quantum stealth transport
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yume-gui
[
.I options
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yume-gui
is an optional Dear ImGui desktop application in the explicit
transport-v2 reference build.
It embeds the same facade sessions used by automation and tests: a
.BR yumed-v2-reference (8)
server controller and a linked, in-process
.BR yume-v2-reference (1)
client runtime.
.PP
The GUI does not reimplement the transport stack.
JSON profiles written here are compatible with the transport-v2
reference CLI binaries.
Native YTP/1 and schema-1 configuration integration remain unfinished.
.SH WORKSPACES
The sidebar switches between two workspaces:
.TP
.B Client
Connect, security, logs, settings, and credits for the
.BR yume-v2-reference (1)
runtime.
.TP
.B Server
Server control, authorized keys, logs, settings, and credits for
.BR yumed-v2-reference (8).
.SH PAGES
.TP
.B Dashboard
Connection summary and quick status for the active workspace.
.TP
.B Connect
Server host, identity key, SOCKS port, stealth toggles, and connect /
disconnect controls.
.TP
.B Security
Inner crypto, TLS profile, obfs secret, and trust material (CA pins,
operator CA import).
.TP
.B Server
Listen port, TLS cert paths, auth keys, real HTTP facade, and daemon
start/stop.
.TP
.B Keys
Generate composite Ed25519 + ML-DSA-87 identities and manage
.B authorized_keys
entries.
.TP
.B Logs
Live log view for the embedded client or server session.
.TP
.B Settings
Appearance (theme), paths, and runtime preferences.
.TP
.B Credits
Project version and license notice.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --headless
Run a no-window facade diagnostic.
It validates existing configuration files and attempts start/stop for
valid profiles.
The current command still exits successfully when profiles are absent or
a valid session fails to start, so it does not by itself verify a
working connection.
.TP
.B --start-minimized
Open hidden.
Use the tray menu (when available) to show the main window.
.TP
.B --no-tray
Disable the system tray icon at runtime even when the build includes
tray support.
.TP
.BI "--client-config " path
Load the client JSON profile from
.I path
instead of the platform default.
.TP
.BI "--server-config " path
Load the server JSON profile from
.I path
instead of the platform default.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Print a help summary and exit.
.SH KEYBOARD AND WINDOW
Standard Dear ImGui navigation applies: click fields to edit, Tab to
move focus, Enter to activate buttons.
The main window can be resized; the sidebar layout adapts to narrow
widths.
.PP
There is no global accelerator table yet.
Use the sidebar to switch pages.
.SH DEVELOPMENT STATUS
The dev6 GUI compiles and links, but it is not yet a qualified frontend.
Shared client/server lifecycle serialization, prompt pre-ready
cancellation, and atomic configuration replacement are covered by
core/facade tests.
Obsolete inner-crypto controls/status, the GUI page's detached resolver
lifetime, partial chat/log delivery, honest headless failure behavior,
and a real window-level connect/stop/reconnect test remain GUI-owned
work.
Use the CLI for supported automation and do not treat
.B --headless
as release evidence.
.SH SYSTEM TRAY
When tray support is compiled in and not disabled with
.BR --no-tray ,
a status icon may appear in the desktop environment's notification area.
.PP
On Wayland (KDE Plasma, GNOME with certain compositors), tray behavior
depends on the desktop portal and StatusNotifier implementation.
If the icon is missing, run with
.B --no-tray
and keep the main window visible, or use the CLI binaries directly.
.SH BUILD
Build the GUI in a separate CMake reference tree with
.BR YUME_BUILD_TRANSPORT_V2=ON ,
.B YUME_BUILD_NATIVE_APPLICATION=OFF
and
.BR YUME_BUILD_GUI=ON .
The reference graph remains uninstalled.
See
.B CONTRIBUTING.md
for dependency setup.
.PP
The GUI requires OpenGL, GLFW, and ImGui/ImPlot fetched by CMake.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.yume/client.json
Default GUI client profile (Linux).
macOS and Windows use the platform-specific config directory under the
user home.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/server.json
Default GUI server configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/secure-materials/
Imported operator CAs, client auth keys, TLS CAs, and external proof
keys.
The metadata uses schema 1 and 32-character random hex IDs.
File paths are derived from each record's ID and material type.
.TP
.I ~/.yume/keys/
Default key generation directory.
